  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "direct judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The spectral and coordinate assertions match. The outstanding issue is the scope of the propagation conclusion, not an unidentified Lean operator or a vacuous premise. The supplied source leaves that scope insufficiently specified for unconditional acceptance.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 3 connects a complete real eigenvector family to component-wave speeds. The target's final conjunct conditions translation and reconstruction on Differentiable Real (Function.uncurry q)."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The blind translation accurately reconstructs the target, including the distinction between pointwise partial derivatives and global joint differentiability. Its uncertainty about the reverse implication can be resolved affirmatively; uncertainty about full source coverage remains.",
      "primary_evidence": "The blind and direct elaborated types have the same quantifier and conjunction structure after replacing LocalDef001–LocalDef003 with D001–D003."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Retain undetermined because Lean-implies-source remains unclear. This follows from the unresolved source solution class, independently of the direct judge's classification.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed pages 1–3 give partial differential equations and translated profiles but no explicit global joint differentiability convention. Methodology section 2 assigns undetermined when Lean-implies-source is unclear."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Retain undetermined, while resolving source-implies-translation to yes. One unresolved implication still prevents either accepted classification.",
      "primary_evidence": "The translated formulas follow for differentiable solutions from the source's real eigenbasis setting and ordinary calculus; their coverage of every source-intended wave remains unspecified."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D013 unclear",
      "resolution": "D013's meaning is understood: joint real differentiability at every point of the whole space-time plane, without continuity of the derivative. Its source applicability, rather than its declaration semantics, remains unclear.",
      "primary_evidence": "D013 unfolds to ∀ x, DifferentiableAt Real f x. D025 sends (x,t) to q x t; the explicit target supplies the usual product topology on Real × Real and finite product topology on Fin m → Real."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "The matrix hypotheses match exactly. The separate global joint differentiability premise is a sufficient analytic condition whose status as an inherited source condition cannot be established from the supplied pages.",
      "primary_evidence": "D003 requires real paired eigenvalues and a complete basis, matching printed page 3. D001 requires only the two slice derivatives at each point; the final target conjunct separately introduces D013."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C05 unclear",
      "resolution": "Unique coefficients, scalar decoupling, signed translation, and full reconstruction are all present for the stated differentiable class. Completeness across the source's unspecified solution class remains unresolved. The acoustic spectral example is illustrative rather than an additional required conclusion of the selected general assertion.",
      "primary_evidence": "D034 is the basis representation followed by conversion to finite coordinate functions; D035 supplies the corresponding basis vectors. The final target conjunct includes both coordinate translation and the sum over every basis index."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "No matrix-field, dimension, spectral-multiplicity, or speed-sign specialization is present. The explicit propagation theorem selects jointly differentiable whole-plane solutions; whether this omits intended source cases remains unresolved and cannot count as stronger coverage.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target quantifies over m : Nat and real matrices, with no distinctness or nonzero-speed premise. Printed page 1 specifies the whole-plane state type but does not specify the joint differentiability condition."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "Algebraic existence, invertibility, and unique expansion are preserved. The target determines solutions within its stated class from their initial trace but does not assert arbitrary-data existence. No separate Cauchy existence theorem is required by the selected sentence; the analytic class remains uncertain.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 3 explicitly asserts unique eigenvector expansion. D033–D035 provide a basis and invertible coefficient representation. The target quantifies an existing q and uses q at time zero."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "The translation correctly reports every actual hypothesis. The unresolved issue is whether the source intends the additional regularity as part of its solution convention, not whether the translation introduced it.",
      "primary_evidence": "Both the exact target and translation put global joint differentiability only before the characteristic and reconstruction conclusions. Neither places it before the pointwise PDE equivalence."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C05 unclear",
      "resolution": "The translated conclusions match all target conjuncts and the source's algebraic content. Full propagation coverage remains conditional on resolving the source solution concept.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 1 identifies propagation with a translated profile; printed page 3 identifies each component speed with its eigenvalue. The translation gives u_i(x,t) = u_i(x − λ_i t,0), followed by reconstruction."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C07 unclear",
      "resolution": "Resolve the relation check itself to pass. Exact equality and the pointwise biconditional are appropriate for invertible eigenbasis diagonalization. The remaining uncertainty concerns applicability and belongs to the hypothesis and coverage checks.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001 and D002 require actual derivative witnesses. Applying the fixed coordinate isomorphism gives c_b(q_t + A q_x)_i = (u_i)_t + λ_i(u_i)_x; invertibility recovers the vector equation from all scalar equations."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "The translation contains no hidden additional specialization beyond the target's explicitly stated analytic class. Dimension zero is a harmless empty case and does not justify a stronger classification.",
      "primary_evidence": "D019–D023 enumerate all Fin m indices, including the empty enumeration when m = 0. Positive dimensions remain universally quantified, and the source states no numerical lower bound for m."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "The translation preserves basis uniqueness and the conditional determination from initial trace. Neither uniqueness of the eigenbasis nor unrestricted solution existence is asserted. Only the source's analytic scope remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "The source says expansion is unique relative to the corresponding eigenvectors. The target chooses a basis existentially before q and uses its coordinate equivalence throughout."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left implication lean_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "Retain unclear for the unrestricted source claim. The target supplies the announced propagation on its differentiable class, but its pointwise equivalence does not by itself establish translation for less regular source-intended waves.",
      "primary_evidence": "The pointwise biconditional concludes scalar derivative equations. The distinct final implication concludes translation only after a global joint differentiability premise; printed pages 1–3 do not delimit the intended solution class."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication translation_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "Retain unclear for the same source-scope reason. There is no additional discrepancy between the translation and Lean that could resolve or worsen this implication.",
      "primary_evidence": "The translation explicitly restricts characteristic formulas to everywhere jointly differentiable solutions, exactly as the target does. Printed page 1 discusses profiles without an explicit differentiability qualification."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear",
      "resolution": "Resolve to yes. The source's finite real eigenbasis setting supports every translated conclusion on the expressly restricted differentiable class. An unspecified broader source class does not obstruct this direction.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed pages 1 and 3 supply q_t + A q_x = 0 and a complete real eigenvector family. In its basis, A is diagonal. Existing slice derivatives transform in both directions under the fixed linear isomorphism. For jointly differentiable q, the derivative of s ↦ u_i(x − λ_i t + λ_i s,s) is (u_i)_t + λ_i(u_i)_x = 0. Constancy between s = 0 and s = t gives the target translation; basis expansion gives reconstruction."
    },
    {
      "item": "Nonvacuity, repeated speeds, and purported stronger coverage",
      "resolution": "The theorem has substantive nonconstant positive-dimensional instances. Repeated, zero, and negative speeds are admitted. Explicit formulas and a biconditional do not establish genuine stronger coverage while the applicability question remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "For m = 1 and A = [a], q(x,t) = x − at satisfies D001 and D013 with the standard eigenbasis; a ≠ 0 gives a moving nonconstant profile. The target never divides by a speed or requires distinct eigenvalues. D004–D005 supply continuity of scalar multiplication, not an impossible condition on q."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "unclear",
      "reasoning": "The target gives a complete real eigenbasis, unique coefficients, exact scalar decoupling, and signed translation with reconstruction for globally jointly differentiable solutions. These recover the selected correspondence on that class. The attached source pages do not establish that this class exhausts the intended component waves: equation (1.3) describes profiles without a regularity qualification, and the general construction is deferred to Chapter 3. Neither a broader weak-solution interpretation nor an exclusively jointly differentiable interpretation should be imposed without evidence."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "A complete independent real eigenvector family in R^m provides the required basis and paired real speeds. Its fixed coordinate isomorphism diagonalizes A and transports existing slice derivatives in both directions, yielding the pointwise biconditional with derivative existence included. For the globally jointly differentiable solutions quantified by the final conjunct, the chain rule makes every characteristic coordinate constant along lines of slope λ_i. Evaluating at time zero gives u_i(x,t) = u_i(x − λ_i t,0), and the basis representation yields the finite reconstruction. These consequences require no decision about additional nonsmooth source cases."
    }
  },
  "classification": "undetermined",
  "accepted": false,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "The supplied primary-source pages do not settle whether the selected general propagation assertion is confined to globally jointly differentiable classical solutions or includes less regular component waves. Consequently full Lean-implies-source coverage cannot be certified."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "unresolved-propagation-applicability",
      "evidence": "Printed pages 1–3 leave the solution regularity convention unspecified. D001 and D002 express actual slice derivatives, whereas the target separately requires D013, global joint differentiability, for translation and reconstruction.",
      "impact": "Acceptance remains unestablished. If broader solution classes are intended, this is reduced applicability; it must not be reclassified as faithful-stronger merely because the classical conclusion is explicit."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "reverse-implication-resolved",
      "evidence": "The source's complete real eigenvector family diagonalizes the constant matrix. Ordinary finite-dimensional differentiation and constancy along characteristics establish precisely the target's restricted analytic conclusions.",
      "impact": "Source-implies-Lean is affirmative; the round-trip judge's uncertainty in this direction is unnecessary."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "spectral-semantics-and-nonvacuity",
      "evidence": "D003 and D033–D035 retain complete paired eigendata and unique basis coefficients. The displacement is x − speeds i * t. Positive-dimensional nonconstant differentiable solutions satisfy the hypotheses.",
      "impact": "No spectral, sign, coordinate-identity, or vacuity defect was found. These checks do not resolve the remaining source-class uncertainty."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The attached primary-source images and exact inline declarations support the same finite real hyperbolic system and signed component-wave mechanism. The blind translation preserves the target's semantics. Independent implication analysis resolves source-implies-Lean affirmatively and separates the understood meaning of Differentiable from its uncertain source applicability. The evidence does not settle the opposite implication over the source's full intended solution class, so undetermined is the consistent classification. No tools, target proof, or external evidence were used, and source or rendering hashes were not independently recomputed."
}
